# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AgreeGate environment
# Copy this file to ".env.local" and fill in what you want.
# Hacker News works with NO setup. Reddit & X are optional add-ons.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Reddit (the primary source). Create a "script" app at:
#   https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps  ->  "create another app..."
#   - type: script
#   - redirect uri (for "Connect Reddit" login): http://localhost:3000/api/auth/reddit/callback
# Then copy the client id (under the app name) and the secret here.
# These power BOTH anonymous app-only search AND optional user login.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: override the OAuth redirect URI. By default it is derived from
# the request origin (e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app/api/auth/reddit/callback).
# Reddit allows ONE redirect URI per app, so it must match the deployed URL.
# REDDIT_REDIRECT_URI=

# Secret used to encrypt the session cookie for logged-in Reddit users.
# Set a long random string in production (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
SESSION_SECRET=

# X / Twitter (secondary, off by default because of heavy bot noise).
# Get a Bearer Token from the X Developer Portal: https://developer.x.com
X_BEARER_TOKEN=
